<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n111211" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῐλό-κᾰλος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>loving the beautiful</i>
			(both of personal and moral beauty), <i>loving beauty and goodness,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				248d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Criti.</u>
				111e
			</span></i>, <i>Com.Adesp. Oxy.</i><i><span class="en">
				1239.18
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ φ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.61d
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				1026d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>fond of effect and elegance,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				1.3.3
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. περὶ ὅπλα</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				2.1.22
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ περὶ τὴν ἐσθῆτα φ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					1.26
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				10.57
			</span></i>; of the peacock, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				488b24
			</span></i>. Adv., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-λως ἔχειν περί τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					12.2.1
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				14.218
			</span></i>, etc.: 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-καλώτερον κοπρίσαι</span>”
				<i>more elaborately,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gp.
					5.26.10
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>fond of honour, seeking honour,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλοκαλώτεροι ἐν τοῖς κινδύνοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					4.15
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1125b12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1179b9
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ τὸ φ. πειραθέντα κατανοῆσαι</span>
			to see by <i>working out the calculation,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Iamb.
				<u>in Nic.</u>
				p.124
			</span></i> P.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
